## 13. Appendix A - departmental pre-reads (circulated 11 November, summarised by Zuzanna)

**A.1 Fleet & Maintenance (Gunnar).** The pool is 126 reefer trailers and 38 tractor units. Five vehicles are older than 12 years, and the oldest tractor is the Volvo known as "Mała Berta", fleet no. 42. Planned maintenance compliance is 94.2 % (target 95 %). Unplanned breakdowns from January to October 2024 numbered 61 against 74 in the same period of 2023, and the average recovery time per breakdown was 3 hours 10 minutes, which Gunnar wants under 2 hours 30 minutes by the end of 2025. Tyre spend year to date is 212,000 EUR. The tyre-pressure sensor (TPMS) retrofit covers 28 units so far. The diesel decision, which is on the parking lot, is that no new diesel tractor units are ordered after 2026 unless a customer pays the difference.

**A.2 Quality & Compliance (Benedikta).** Customer complaints from January to October 2024 numbered 83 against 69 in the same period last year; 11 of them concern alerting. The average closure time is 6.4 working days against a target of 5. Two corrective actions are open from the Helvetia audit. Internal audits completed: 17 of 18 planned (the 18th, at KLJ-5, was moved to January 2025 because the yard manager was ill). In the pharma lanes 98.6 % of KC-Tag 4 loggers are within their 12-month calibration window; the remaining 1.4 % are 20 tags that Benedikta will have recalibrated before the Helvetia list goes out.

**A.3 Legal (Sofia).** Seventeen customer contracts come up for renewal in 2025. Three customers have asked to bring their excursion-credit tables in line with the new Oakhaven wording; Sofia's position is that nothing is offered unprompted and nothing is refused without Priya. The EU trade mark application for the word mark Tidewalk was granted on 9 October 2024. The NDA template moved to version 3 in September. The legal hold from July remains open.

**A.4 People & Culture (Ines).** Open positions at 1 November: 19. Average time to hire over the last 12 months: 47 days (target 40). Training hours per head year to date: 11.8 (target 16). Sick leave rate in operations: 5.1 % (company: 3.6 %). Eight new starters joined in October, six of them in Gdynia operations.

**A.5 IT & Support (Kamil, via Tomasz).** Support tickets per month averaged 1,380 from July to October; first response within 30 minutes in 91 % of cases. The platform met its monthly availability target in July, September and October but not in August, which is the month of the two incidents.

## 14. Appendix B - rooms, dinner and the bus

Rooms 1 to 12 in the main building were allocated alphabetically except that Marta had the corner room 1 and Dieter room 2 ("so that he can hear the lake"). The dinner on Thursday was a three-course menu at 78 EUR per head (wine not included; wine came to 640 EUR in total, which Priya has agreed to expense in this one case). The vegetarian options were requested by Benedikta, Sofia and Ines; Tomasz asked for no mushrooms. Dr Kroll's invoice (2,950 EUR per day for two days plus 410 EUR travel) will be paid on 30 days. The bus company charged 690 EUR for the return trip, and the driver's tip of 50 EUR came out of the kitty jar after all.

The meeting closed at 14:25 on Friday. Marta thanked everybody, the kitty jar went to the Villa staff, and the bus left at 15:30 as planned. Pan Zenon was on time for the return trip, which Rafał called "suspicious".

Zuzanna Frąckowiak, 26 November 2024.
